00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.120
It's not the WK's opinion, it's my opinion.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:13.120
They're 40 against 1.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:14.720
South Africa is bleeding.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.840
And this is why we have to train our people.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.480
To be prepared.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:22.960
For any attack anywhere.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.240
So all you do is you move forward the whole time.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.240
Push! You move forward.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:28.960
Move forward.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.720
Uh uh. No.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.120
Don't try and be clever now.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:41.120
It's just speed that helps.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.280
I'm not strong. Check out these skinny arms!

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.520
Sergeant, do it again. We didn't see!
- It's speed that counts.

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:46.720
No, no, no! Please!

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.320
My head.

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.640
Number one, what did you learn today?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.360
How to take a gun from someone's hands.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.760
Like from someone who's attacking you.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.000
Do you think you'd be able to do it in the real world?

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:58.880
Yes.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:14.480
Again!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.160
Right on the left flank.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.280
Right turn!

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:18.640
One, two, three.

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:19.440
One!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.320
The lesson I am going to give you today is surely

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.000
the most important lesson,

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.160
the enemy and the threat

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.920
You cannot live in this country if
you don't know who your enemy is.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.920
Who are the people who stand against us?

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.880
Who are the people threatening
our lives in this country?

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.960
Who are these animals?

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.560
And you must tell me.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:46.480
Black people, Colonel.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.960
You said it, not me.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:52.560
There's a conflict between
white people and black people in this country.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:54.000
We must accept this.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:56.000
Why is there a conflict?

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:57.440
Number one.

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:01.520
There's an external conflict. We look different.
We don't look the same as each other.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:06.880
They have thick lips.
The lips are likely to curl upwards.

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:10.160
Okay? We have thin lips.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.560
You laugh, but it's the truth.
You see it every day.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:18.000
The negroes ears on the inside
are totally different to ours.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.520
It's much more sensitive.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:23.040
That's why us Afrikaners know, hit them
against the ears and they'll fall to the ground.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.280
Because their ears are made differently.

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:31.520
I don't know why we were being
taught about their noses.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:35.520
If you have big ears,
does that make you someone else?

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:36.400
No.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.640
Let's see what Dr. Carlton Putnam has to say.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.200
Respected anthropologist. He says,

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:45.200
..clearly indicated that the negroes inferiority
to the white man,

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:47.680
average against average,

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:48.880
in many ways,

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:54.240
but in no way more significantly than in
the size and the weight of the brain,

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:58.400
especially in the measurements
of the brain's frontal cortex."

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:00.320
Your cortex is your forebrain.

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:03.200
Your forebrain is responsible for planning.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.480
Your forebrain helps you take initiative.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:12.320
Your forebrain helps you remember things,

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.160
to remember intsructions.

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.520
and to serve.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:21.680
That's why there is not one country
in Africa that is a First-World Country.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:23.600
Now we ask ourselves,

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.000
is there a difference in the intelligence levels
between a negro and a caucasian?

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.360
Dr Albert Schweitzer,

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:34.560
"One must look at the negro
not as one's equal, but as a child.

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:38.080
And with children,
nothing can be done without authority."

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:41.120
A black man has the intelligence level
of a 14-year-old white boy.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.080
Dr Meredith Townsend says,

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:48.160
"Negroes have never advanced
out of the foulest savagery."

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.640
This is why they will kill you for nothing.

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.200
They have no moral values.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:56.240
You need to know, who is the enemy?
Who will attack me?

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:57.440
How he looks.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.680
It's not my fault he's black.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.000
Colonel Jooste is a very clever man.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.960
I didn't know he was that clever,

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.880
but he's terribly smart.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:09.360
I don't believe something straight off the bat.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:14.720
I'm very inquisitive, so I won't
accept anything he tells me right then and there.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:19.920
I will do research to see if it is the truth.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:21.440
This all information

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:25.040
that the press and international media
say you mustn't know.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:26.640
They keep it away from you.

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.720
They smother it so that you don't know.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:31.440
And the only place you'll hear it is here.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.760
You won't hear it anywhere else.

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:39.040
You get black people that are extremist,
and you get white people that are extremist.

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:43.280
So on each side you have extremists,

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:46.400
the middle and the other extremists.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.920
They are in conflict with each other,
and the middle group goes along like sheep.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.480
I'm not an extremist, so I'm one of the sheep.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.560
I find the new South Africa...

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:11.920
difficult.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:15.360
There are difficult circumstances for us whites.

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:17.200
Especially to get work.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:23.600
I, myself, am not chosen first for a position
that may be open at the mines,

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:32.960
because it's first the non-whites. Then his wife,
then his children. Then is it us.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.000
We're last.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:38.160
We eat off the ground, on our knees.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:48.880
The Border War took place between 1966 and 1989.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:52.640
And every young man had to go to the Border.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:58.560
Most South African families had a brother,
a father or son on the Border.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.840
So what now?

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.200
This!

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:06.480
This is the path that we must follow.

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:12.320
The training that you receive, the standard of
that training, is the same as what you just saw.

00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:15.920
The path that we follow is the same
as the path that those men walked.

00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:19.520
Nkosi sikelel' iafrika?

00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:23.760
Don't go down that path.

00:22:26.960 --> 00:22:29.440
What happened was, we went in,

00:22:29.440 --> 00:22:32.320
we got orders to go in and go sweep.

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:37.600
Our first vehicle set off a land mine.

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:43.280
What happens when you set off a landmine is that
the doors fall open and you jump out.

00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:46.000
And when we jumped out they were waiting for us.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.320
Then they hit us.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.880
When I hit they ground they shot me.

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:58.320
About three or four guys away,

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:01.120
my friend was shot through the head.

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:04.240
Dead.

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:08.640
Can you see it?

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:14.000
When we...

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:21.440
They shot me here.

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:34.880
Men.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:37.600
You think we're all talk.

00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.720
Now you've seen an example,

00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:43.440
of what really happened,

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:46.400
to a man here with us.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:50.560
This man's life at that stage,

00:23:51.680 --> 00:23:54.560
was hanging on a thread finer than a hair.

00:23:55.680 --> 00:24:00.000
This is why I lose my mind sometimes
when it comes to your training.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:06.080
Because if we had not been trained,
or it had been you out there,

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:07.360
no one would have survived

00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:11.760
You need to have discipline.
Discipline, discipline, discipline!

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:15.920
Because if you don't have discipline,
you can't execute an operation such as that.

00:24:29.600 --> 00:24:31.200
If we're sitting around the camp fire one day,

00:24:31.200 --> 00:24:33.600
no one can say,

00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:36.560
you weren't in the army
and you didn't get this type of training,

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:38.800
I can say I've had this training...

00:24:38.800 --> 00:24:41.680
but only for nine days, not for three months!

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:44.960
So yes. It's also something to be proud of,

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:46.080
if you can make it through.

00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:48.880
Yes it's hard, but it makes you proud.

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:51.840
Everything we do, our dads did.

00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:54.320
It was hard for them also and they always say..

00:24:55.440 --> 00:24:57.520
we did it, we went to the army.

00:24:58.800 --> 00:25:06.560
So this is kind of the same and now we've
done it so we can say we've done it as well.

00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:10.880
Finishing this camp will make
me feel more like a man.

00:25:10.880 --> 00:25:12.720
I can talk to my dad who was in the army

00:25:12.720 --> 00:25:15.360
about what he's been through because
I've been through it as well..

00:25:16.400 --> 00:25:17.440
in nine days.

00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:18.640
My father?

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:22.000
My father is dead.

00:25:22.960 --> 00:25:26.800
He was a big guy, and he drank a lot.

00:25:27.280 --> 00:25:28.800
He got his life sorted out,

00:25:28.800 --> 00:25:31.280
he gave his heart to the Lord.

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:36.000
He started coming right but it was too late
for him and my mom to try again.

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:40.320
But he did turn his life around,
so I can turn my life around as well,

00:25:40.320 --> 00:25:44.080
and I can discipline my son in a
way he'll never forget,

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:46.720
if he ever even tries any of that shit.

00:25:47.440 --> 00:25:50.560
That's the difference, I didn't have a dad.

00:26:16.400 --> 00:26:20.640
I'm tired. We sleep three hours a day.

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:39.120
Sergeant Carstens smokes tobacco, ahum!

00:26:41.520 --> 00:26:45.440
Sergeant Carstens smokes tobacco, ahum!

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:52.240
Those songs, I'm teaching them those.

00:26:52.240 --> 00:26:55.360
Sergeant Carstens smokes tobacco

00:26:55.360 --> 00:26:59.040
and sits on his ass the whole day, ahum!

00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:03.920
Ahum! Ahum! Chicky bum, chicky bubblegum!

00:27:03.920 --> 00:27:05.600
I have to fucking teach it to them

00:27:05.600 --> 00:27:06.960
because we have nothing fun to do here.

00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:11.360
and they ask me all the time for a bunch of shit.

00:27:12.240 --> 00:27:16.560
But it's also actually to help
keep their minds off the KFC,

00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:21.760
and the damn Steers burgers and
whatever the hell else they're craving.

00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:25.520
We find him at the Magistrate. ahum!

00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:30.800
We find him at the Magistrate, ahum!

00:27:32.640 --> 00:27:36.640
We find him at the Magistrate, the Magistrate

00:27:36.640 --> 00:27:38.960
he pulls my leg, ahum!

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:40.640
Barnard is small.

00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:43.440
He's really small so we don't really listen to what he says.

00:27:43.440 --> 00:27:45.040
He sometimes says silly things.

00:27:45.920 --> 00:27:46.960
Stupid things.

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:48.560
The Colonel's coming!

00:27:49.360 --> 00:27:50.880
He tries to fit in.

00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:54.160
But he'll fit in if he stops trying so hard.

00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:58.160
He just needs to relax and be himself

00:27:58.400 --> 00:28:00.480
